{{!
    @template theme_diverse/login_brand

    Brand panel shown next to the login form on large screens (hidden on small screens).
    DIVERSE and each partner chosen in the "Select Partner" menu get the same panel: their photo
    (or the landing page's photo), their name and one sentence. A partner's panel ends with a link to DIVERSE.

    Context variables:
    * name, intro - title and sentence of the panel
    * photourl - optional photo filling the panel
    * ispartner - whether a partner is chosen
    * homeurl - DIVERSE site home
    * brandsjson - optional (signup page): name, intro, photourl and ispartner of DIVERSE ("0") and of each partner
      by id, so that the panel follows the university chosen in the form (core_renderer::SIGNUP_BRAND_JS)

    The way back to the site home stays in the top left corner of the page, also where the panel is hidden.

    The photo and the link are always in the markup, hidden when not used, so that the signup page can switch
    between partners.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "name": "Technische Hochschule Rosenheim", "intro": "Log in with your account.",
        "photourl": "", "ispartner": true, "homeurl": "#"
    }
}}
<a class="diverse-login-back" href="{{homeurl}}"><i class="fa fa-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{#str}}login_back, theme_diverse{{/str}}</a>
<aside class="diverse-login-brand{{#photourl}} diverse-login-brand-photo{{/photourl}}" aria-label="{{name}}"{{#brandsjson}} data-brands="{{brandsjson}}"{{/brandsjson}}>
    <img class="diverse-login-photo" {{#photourl}}src="{{photourl}}"{{/photourl}}{{^photourl}}hidden{{/photourl}} alt="">
    <div class="diverse-login-brand-body">
        <p class="diverse-login-brand-title">{{name}}</p>
        <p class="diverse-login-brand-intro">{{intro}}</p>
    </div>
    <a class="diverse-login-brand-member" href="{{homeurl}}"{{^ispartner}} hidden{{/ispartner}}>{{#str}}login_partner_member, theme_diverse{{/str}}</a>
</aside>
